# Get a free key at https://www.pexels.com/api/
# Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder (the repo root) and put your key
# in it. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed, so never put a real key
# here.
#
# The key is a single long string with no spaces, quotes or braces —
# roughly 56 characters of letters and numbers.
#
# NOTE ON KEY HANDLING
# Pexels has no OAuth / no server-side token exchange, so a browser-only app
# must ship the key to the client. The SDK is designed so this is the ONLY
# place the key appears: `configureMedia({ apiKey })` hands it to the transport
# layer and nothing else in the codebase ever reads it. In production you would
# point `baseUrl` at your own proxy and drop the key entirely -- see
# packages/media-core/README.md, "Auth".
VITE_PEXELS_API_KEY=your_pexels_api_key_here
